\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Plain SHAP attributions for instance $X=1, M=1, Y=1$. For target $X$, plain SHAP assigns $\phi _Y = 0.139 > 0$, even though $Y$ does not cause $X$. This arises because $v(\{Y\}) = 0.778 > 0.5$: observing $Y=1$ is statistically informative about $X=1$ through the chain $X \to M \to Y$. SHAP cannot distinguish ``$Y$ is informative about $X$'' from ``$Y$ causes $X$'' because the value function is grounded in observational conditionals, which are symmetric under reversal of causal direction. }}{23}{table.caption.13}\protected@file@percent }
